;; posix's functions whose system call takes a pointer (queue 231; Modules/posixmodule.c and resource.c, function by
;; function): the buffer's address is reflect's Pointer of a Go slice or pointer kept alive across the call, as mmap's
;; msync and isatty's ioctl take it (queue 220), so the class :pointer-syscall narrows to nothing of these. timerfd's,
;; tcgetpgrp and tcsetpgrp, unshare and setns, memfd_create, sched_getaffinity and sched_setaffinity, the xattr
;; functions and resource.prlimit. unshare and setns run on every thread of the process (AllThreadsSyscall): Python's
;; main thread is a goroutine that may run on any of Go's threads, and /proc/self is the thread group leader's, so the
;; change must hold on all of them for the calling thread's view to be the one C gives; CLONE_NEWUSER and the like, which
;; need a single-threaded process, fail as Go says (EINVAL).


